# Web3Forms access key for the contact form.
# Get one free at https://web3forms.com (enter your email, no account needed).
#
# This value is PUBLIC — Vite inlines VITE_* variables into the client bundle.
# Web3Forms treats it as a submission token, not a credential, so that is expected.
# Spam protection comes from the honeypot field in ConnectSection.jsx.
#
# Copy to .env for local development. For the deployed site, add it as a GitHub
# Actions repository secret named VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY (Settings → Secrets and
# variables → Actions), which .github/workflows/deploy.yml passes to the build.
#
# If this is unset, the form falls back to opening the visitor's mail client.
VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
